          "title": "You'll want to know: व्यथते",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "व्यथते — vyathate — \"is pained; is distressed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मित्रस्य दुःखेन मीरा व्यथते। mitrasya duḥkhena mīrā vyathate. Mira is pained by her friend's sorrow."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (she …): सा व्यथितवती, sā vyathitavatī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "व्यथते (vyathate) comes from the root √vyath, \"to tremble\"; MW's ppp vyathita is \"disquieted, distressed, afflicted\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
